> import docs
> help docs
module docs
  Small numerical helpers.
  Used by the REPL help tests.
  exports: norm2, trapz, undocumented, LVParams
> help docs.norm2
norm2(v: vector): real
  Euclidean norm of a real or complex vector.
  Returns a real scalar.
> help docs.trapz
trapz(f, a: real, b: real; n: int = 100): real
  Integrates f from a to b with n trapezoids.

  The keyword n sets the number of panels.
> help docs.undocumented
undocumented(x)
  (no documentation)
> help docs.LVParams
record LVParams(a: real, b: real)
  Parameters of the Lotka-Volterra model.
> help docs.hidden
ImportError: module "docs" has no exported name "hidden"
  at <repl>:1:1
> from docs import norm2
> help norm2
norm2(v: vector): real
  Euclidean norm of a real or complex vector.
  Returns a real scalar.
> import attached
> help attached
module attached
  (no documentation)
  exports: double
> help attached.double
double(x: matrix{real}): matrix{real}
  Doubles x. This block opens the file but has no blank line after it,
  so it documents the function, not the module.
> import linalg
> help linalg.solve
solve(A, b)
  The solution of A x = b for square A (the same as A \ b).
> help sqrt
sqrt(x)
  The square root (NaN for a negative real; use a complex argument)
> help print
print(a, b, ...)
  Writes the values separated by spaces, then a newline
